-- title:
--   Second inequality for quadratic extensions: index divides 2
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $E$ be number fields with $E$ a $k$-algebra of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_k E = 2$, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_k$. Work in the group of invertible fractional ideals of $k$, and let $I_k(\mathfrak f) =$ `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣` be its subgroup of those $I$ whose valuation `FractionalIdeal.count` at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_k$ dividing $\mathfrak f$ vanishes. Two subgroups are compared with it: first, `narrowRaySubgroup k 𝔣`, generated by the principal fractional ideals $(\alpha)$ with $\alpha \in \mathcal O_k$, $\alpha \neq 0$, $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak f$ and $\tau(\alpha) > 0$ for every ring homomorphism $\tau : k \to \mathbb R$; second, the image of `coprimeToModulus E (𝔣.map (algebraMap (𝓞 k) (𝓞 E)))` under the homomorphism sending an invertible fractional ideal $J$ of $E$ to the finite product $\prod_w \mathfrak p_{w\cap\mathcal O_k}^{\,f(w)\cdot \operatorname{count}_w(J)}$, where $f(w)$ is the inertia degree `inertiaDeg'` of $w$ over the prime below it — that is, the relative norm of $J$. Each of the two subgroups is intersected with $I_k(\mathfrak f)$ (`subgroupOf`); the assertion is that the index in $I_k(\mathfrak f)$ of the subgroup generated by these two intersections divides $2$.
--
--   This is the ideal-theoretic second inequality of global class field theory in the case of a quadratic extension, stated at an arbitrary modulus $\mathfrak f$ with no admissibility hypothesis: the narrow ray group together with the relative norms of ideals prime to $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_E$ has index $1$ or $2$ among the ideals of $k$ prime to $\mathfrak f$. It is the quadratic instance used by [`M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut`](thm.html#M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut), and it is deduced from the cyclic-extension input [`HeckeCharacter.ideleFirstIneqDataAt_of_isCyclic`](thm.html#HeckeCharacter.ideleFirstIneqDataAt_of_isCyclic), degree $2$ dividing $24$.
-- source:
